```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class CompoundInterest {
    // Compound interest, rounded to two decimal places
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter principal, rate per cent and time in years:");
        double p = sc.nextDouble();
        double r = sc.nextDouble();
        int t = sc.nextInt();
        double amount = p * Math.pow(1 + r / 100, t);
        double ci = amount - p;
        double shown = Math.round(ci * 100) / 100.0;   // two decimal places
        System.out.println("Compound interest = " + shown);
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `25000 8 3`

**Output:**

```
Enter principal, rate per cent and time in years:
Compound interest = 6492.8
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| p | double | principal |
| r | double | rate per cent per year |
| t | int | time in years |
| amount | double | principal plus interest |
| ci | double | compound interest before rounding |
| shown | double | compound interest rounded to two decimals |

