```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class CubeBox {
    // Side and surface area of a cube from its volume
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter the volume of the cube in cubic cm:");
        double vol = sc.nextDouble();
        double side = Math.cbrt(vol);
        double face = Math.pow(side, 2);
        double surface = 6 * face;
        System.out.println("Side = " + side);
        System.out.println("Area of one face = " + face);
        System.out.println("Total surface area = " + surface);
        System.out.println("Volume check = " + Math.pow(side, 3));
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `343`

**Output:**

```
Enter the volume of the cube in cubic cm:
Side = 7.0
Area of one face = 49.0
Total surface area = 294.0
Volume check = 343.0
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| vol | double | volume of the cube |
| side | double | edge length, cube root of the volume |
| face | double | area of one face |
| surface | double | total surface area, six faces |
